From 1fa968b5a60f83b34e5b7605f7ee55c89f6e8aac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 01:24:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Terminate identity-verified bound processes on
 expiry after failed receipts

TTL/max-runtime now terminate every live exact-identity worker_bound witness of a modern-result run (not only the outer), after verifying all witnesses first: any recycled, unknown or malformed witness holds the whole plan and nothing is signalled. Dead outer with hung bound is covered. Post-kill gate still reserves closure/accounting for the strict atomic finalizer.

Proof: real distinct hung outer/bound, dead-outer/hung-bound and historical-bound processes; RED 14 pass/12 fail against outer-only b9a593c341.
